WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.220
I saw Microsoft is doing layoffs.

00:00:02.220 --> 00:00:04.040
It's pretty stressful.

00:00:04.040 --> 00:00:06.580
I've been through two rounds of layoffs.

00:00:06.580 --> 00:00:09.440
Luckily, I wasn't impacted either time.

00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:10.250
However, I remember those days.

00:00:10.250 --> 00:00:16.020
I remember the lady crying on the sofa, apparently impacted.

00:00:16.020 --> 00:00:19.860
I remember people hugging each other in meeting rooms.

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:22.780
Looks like they were saying goodbye to each other.

00:00:22.780 --> 00:00:24.460
It's pretty hard to watch.

00:00:24.460 --> 00:00:27.880
In big tech, layoffs happen pretty fast.

00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:30.600
You get an email saying your role is impacted,

00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:35.100
and a few hours later, you are locked out of all the systems.

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:35.820
That's it.

00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:39.360
So today, I want to share a small technique

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:44.800
that therapists, counsellors and psychologists introduce to their clients

00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:48.280
to help them manage similar stressful situations.

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:51.480
It's called cognitive defusion.

00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:54.620
Essentially, it's the ability to observe your thoughts

00:00:54.620 --> 00:00:57.840
instead of believing they are reality.

00:00:57.840 --> 00:01:02.720
It's the ability to differentiate reality and imagined emotions.

00:01:02.720 --> 00:01:06.080
Let's use the layoffs as an example.

00:01:06.080 --> 00:01:08.900
When we see the email, "your role is impacted",

00:01:08.900 --> 00:01:10.100
it's very stressful.

00:01:10.100 --> 00:01:15.580
And sometimes there is a chain of thoughts that happens lightning fast in our head.

00:01:15.580 --> 00:01:17.220
I lost my job.

00:01:17.220 --> 00:01:20.520
I won't be able to find a job anytime soon.

00:01:20.520 --> 00:01:20.770
I cannot pay my mortgage.

00:01:20.770 --> 00:01:25.360
I cannot pay my kid's tuition fees.

00:01:25.360 --> 00:01:26.740
My life is miserable.

00:01:26.740 --> 00:01:28.400
All of this happens pretty fast

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:31.960
because the threat centre in our head got triggered.

00:01:31.960 --> 00:01:34.560
And we believe these are reality.

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:38.040
However, if you think about it, none of this has to be true.

00:01:38.040 --> 00:01:40.980
You might get a job pretty soon.

00:01:40.980 --> 00:01:47.240
In fact, a lot of my former colleagues got impacted, found a job pretty soon,

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:49.780
and they even found better jobs.

00:01:49.780 --> 00:01:55.120
In fact, a lot of them advanced their career as a result of being laid off.

00:01:55.120 --> 00:01:58.580
So the key difference is two sentences.

00:01:58.580 --> 00:02:00.700
One is: "I am doomed."

00:02:00.700 --> 00:02:05.420
The other is: "I notice that I have a thought that I am doomed."

00:02:05.420 --> 00:02:07.180
Did you see the difference?

00:02:07.180 --> 00:02:08.330
Saying "I am doomed", you are describing a reality,

00:02:08.330 --> 00:02:12.660
you are describing a fact that you are doomed.

00:02:12.660 --> 00:02:16.200
But when you say "I have a thought: I am doomed",

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:18.180
you are noticing that you have a thought,

00:02:18.180 --> 00:02:18.610
but it might not be true.

00:02:18.610 --> 00:02:22.300
It might be imagined.

00:02:22.300 --> 00:02:27.220
So we can see another example when we are helping our kid with homework.

00:02:27.220 --> 00:02:30.380
Sometimes you see it's so easy and they cannot do it well.

00:02:30.380 --> 00:02:31.960
Sometimes they fight,

00:02:31.960 --> 00:02:34.420
and sometimes I do have the train of thought

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:37.180
that they cannot even do the easy homework.

00:02:37.180 --> 00:02:37.430
What about the hard ones?

00:02:37.430 --> 00:02:38.670
What about exams?

00:02:38.670 --> 00:02:40.070
What about university?

00:02:40.070 --> 00:02:42.680
What about career?

00:02:42.680 --> 00:02:44.920
They might end up having a really bad career.

00:02:44.920 --> 00:02:46.540
That's stressful.

00:02:46.540 --> 00:02:49.060
Now I'm even laughing thinking about this.

00:02:49.060 --> 00:02:51.840
But in that particular moment, you get very stressed

00:02:51.840 --> 00:02:54.680
and you believe your kid is going to have a bad career.

00:02:54.680 --> 00:02:57.080
So using cognitive defusion as a technique,

00:02:57.080 --> 00:03:00.440
we should tell ourselves in that particular moment:

00:03:00.440 --> 00:03:03.300
"I have a thought that my kid is going to have a bad career.

00:03:03.300 --> 00:03:04.700
But this is not a reality,

00:03:04.700 --> 00:03:09.500
because it's something generated by my head in a stressful situation."

00:03:09.500 --> 00:03:13.080
So today I'm sharing this technique called cognitive defusion,

00:03:13.080 --> 00:03:20.180
in the hope that we can use it to deal with the ups and downs that life throws at us.
